* [Method portfolio](method-portfolio.md): question-to-method-to-interpretation map, original broad repertoire and representation alternatives.

## Execution and interpretation boundaries

Adaptive discovery naturally reuses observations. Preserve the discovery archive; freeze a rule or prediction before claiming prospective validation. Hold out base geometries/families when transformed or nearby examples share information. Broad discovery can be exploratory without a predeclared theorem, but searching many quantities changes the weight of a striking correlation. Report selection and inspect fresh discriminating cases.

Retain failure/indeterminate outcomes and costs: conditioning on successful cheap capacity computations can change the population under study. Acquisition must track whether it buys a new geometry, a new feature for an existing geometry, higher-confidence evaluation, or mathematical analysis. These are different costs and scientific actions.

No new data generation or theorem claim was executed in preparing this packet. The component reports below expand alternatives and primary-source connections; their proposals do not certify novelty or feasibility until the named pilot checks it.
